$$kx + 3y = -5$$', NULL, $lyceon_json$[{"key":"A","text":"$-2$"},{"key":"B","text":"$-6$"},{"key":"C","text":"$2$"},{"key":"D","text":"$6$"}]$lyceon_json$::jsonb, 'A', NULL, E'A system has no solution when the lines are parallel (same slope, different intercepts). Rewriting the first equation: $y = \\frac{6}{9}x - \\frac{14}{9} = \\frac{2}{3}x - \\frac{14}{9}$. Rewriting the second: $y = -\\frac{k}{3}x - \\frac{5}{3}$. For equal slopes, $-\\frac{k}{3} = \\frac{2}{3}$, giving $k = -2$. The intercepts $-\\frac{14}{9}$ and $-\\frac{5}{3} = -\\frac{15}{9}$ are different, confirming no solution (parallel, not coincident). Choosing $-6$ results from multiplying both sides by $3$ instead of solving $-\\frac{k}{3} = \\frac{2}{3}$ correctly (i.e., setting $k = -2 \\cdot 3$). Choosing $2$ comes from dropping the negative sign when solving $-\\frac{k}{3} = \\frac{2}{3}$. Choosing $6$ results from equating coefficients of $x$ directly ($k = 6$) without converting to slope-intercept form, which would make the lines intersect rather than be parallel.', $lyceon_json${"A":{"role":"correct","error_taxonomy":null},"B":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"sign_error"},"C":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"sign_error"},"D":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"concept_gap"}}$lyceon_json$::jsonb, NULL, 'draft', 1, 105, false, $lyceon_json${"provenance":"Lyceon original","authored_by":"claude","authored_date":"2026-08-19"}$lyceon_json$::jsonb, $lyceon_json${"model":"claude","generation_date":"2026-08-19","prompt_version":"questions_governance_v1"}$lyceon_json$::jsonb);




